      "topic": "Flows",
      "relevance": "Market-wide",
      "headline": "Foreign investors bought a net ₹6,837 crore of Indian shares on Tuesday, their largest single day in about a year",
      "what": "Provisional exchange data showed foreign institutional investors as net buyers of ₹6,836.81 crore in the cash market on 3 November, a third straight day of net buying, while domestic institutions were net sellers of ₹3,678.85 crore. Business Standard said it was the largest single-day foreign purchase since October 2025.",
      "why": "Foreign portfolio flows move the broad indices and the rupee: PTI linked the rupee's 9-paise gain on Tuesday partly to these inflows. Provisional figures can be revised when NSDL publishes final data.",
