    {
      "topic": "Corporate",
      "relevance": "Market-wide",
      "headline": "State Bank of India's September-quarter net profit rose 14.3% to ₹23,038 crore as bad loans eased",
      "what": "SBI reported on 3 November a standalone net profit of ₹23,038 crore for July to September, 14.3% more than a year earlier. Gross non-performing assets (loans in default) eased to 1.39% of loans, and net NPAs to 0.36%. Advances grew nearly 18%. The shares closed 1.77% lower at ₹969.55 on BSE that day.",
      "why": "SBI is India's largest lender and carries large weights in the Nifty Bank and PSU bank indices, so its loan growth and asset quality are read as a gauge of credit demand and bank balance sheets.",
      "source": {
        "name": "Business Standard",
        "url": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/sbi-q2-fy27-net-profit-nii-provisions-asset-quality-126110300887_1.html"
