    {
      "topic": "Global",
      "relevance": "Market-wide",
      "headline": "Brent settled 1.12% lower at $103.60 as the US and Iran remained apart on a deal, with Qatar mediating",
      "what": "Reuters reported on 3 November that an Iranian official called the US response to Iran's conditions unconvincing, while Qatar said both sides were reviewing its proposals. Brent rose about 1% after reports of overnight US strikes on Iran's Qeshm Island, then settled at $103.60 a barrel, its lowest settlement since 7 October.",
      "why": "India imports most of its crude oil, so oil prices pass through to the import bill, the rupee, fuel costs and inflation.",
