      "headline": "Wall Street ended mixed on US midterm election day as chip shares recovered",
      "what": "On 3 November the S&P 500 rose 0.36% and the Nasdaq Composite 0.83% as semiconductor shares rebounded, while the Dow fell 0.38%. Reuters reported early in Asian hours on 4 November that US stock futures were lower while election results were still coming in; control of Congress had not been confirmed.",
      "why": "The make-up of the US Congress shapes US fiscal, trade and technology policy, which reaches India through foreign portfolio flows, the dollar and US bond yields, and through demand for Indian IT services.",
